\paragraph{Non-independence and ecological inference.}
Types within a batch share prompt context, so their extraction outcomes are not independent---a form of ecological correlation \cite{robinson-1950-ecological}. This non-independence is built into the design: BCS measures batch-level confusability precisely because co-present types interact during type resolution. The core batch-level $R^2 = 0.218\text{--}0.578$ (\S\ref{sec:practical_magnitude}) is a direct empirical observation from regressing batch accuracy on BCS, not derived from the simulation above. The inter-pair SCS correlation $\rho = 0.35$ used in the simulation was estimated from the SCS correlation matrix independently of batch-level accuracy data.

